Subject: [PATCH] feat: Goblin Diplomacy quest; Goblin Village lookout ladder
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

New quest. Progress is the client varbit gobdip_main (2378): 0, 3 started
(orange wanted), 4 blue wanted, 5 brown wanted, 6 complete; Quest Helper
has steps for 0/3, 4 and 5 (starting at 3 is inferred from that). The
three armour crates use gobdip_crate1..3_searched and Grubfoot's look the
multinpc varbit gobdip_grubfoot_vis, so the client and Quest Helper see
them. Dialogue follows the OSRS Wiki transcript (random openers, topic
menu, start, the three try-ons as dialogue). Orange/blue dye on goblin
mail and dye mixing (red+yellow, yellow+blue, red+blue) are one
transaction each. Rewards: 5 QP, 200 Crafting XP, a gold bar.

The goblin-village generals and Grubfoot scripts are folded into the
quest (their dialogue is kept as the no-quest / after-quest talk). The
lookout ladder by the south gate (goblin_ladder_bottom/top) had no
handler; it now climbs between level 0 and level 2.

QuestTalkFixture gains a fixed random value and a generic interact().
Guesses: the journal, the dye-mixing message, and "Human! Get us <colour>
armour!" when asking for a new colour mid-quest.

